/*
  Security headers for static hosts that read a _headers file (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages).

  The Content-Security-Policy is also injected as a meta tag at build time by the cspPlugin in
  vite.config.ts, so the policy travels with the bundle regardless of host. This file exists for
  the headers a meta tag cannot express — frame-ancestors above all — and so the policy is
  enforced at the HTTP layer where it is harder to strip.

  Keep connect-src in sync with vite.config.ts if you change the RPC or relayer origin. The
  values below are the devnet defaults; a mainnet build must be rebuilt with
  VITE_RPC_ENDPOINT and VITE_RELAYER_URL set, which regenerates the meta policy.

  'wasm-unsafe-eval' is mandatory: without it snarkjs cannot compile the withdraw circuit and
  no proof can be generated.
*/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.devnet.solana.com wss://api.devnet.solana.com https://solflare.com; frame-src 'self' https://solflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; worker-src 'self' blob:; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), usb=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
